    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1.Constitution-making body (Parliament) with improved administrative and human resources capacities to undertake drafting, public outreach and consultation and with mechanisms to ensure the participation of women and marginalized groups. 
2. Parliament with improved administrative and human resources capacities to discharge its mandates in relation to law-making, oversight and representation. 
3. Country with strengthened environments for civic engagement, including legal/regulatory framework for civil society organizations to function in the public sphere and contribute to development, and effective mechanisms/platforms to engage civil society (with a focus on women, youth or excluded groups).

Scale 
0=UNDP is not building capacity of Parliament 
1=Capacity has not improved 
2= Capacity very partially improved 
3= Capacity partially improved 
4= Capacity largely improved</narrative>
